  "description": "Canonical corpus for the message-suppression predicate (is_suppressed / is_spam_by_classifier / is_text_blocked). Mirrors the webapp's isSpamByClassifier (decision order: disabled -> promoted hash -> demoted hash -> hidden tags -> hide_auto_beacons -> min_info_score) combined with the unconditional isTextBlocked half of passesBaseGuards. Hide semantics over multi-label tags (classifier unification, Q1): a message carrying `qso` is hidden iff `qso` is hidden; a message without `qso` is hidden iff any of its tags is hidden; `auto_beacon` is an ordinary hideable tag. A policy without a `hiddenTags` key falls back to the default [time, bot]; an explicit empty list hides nothing. Field names in `policies` and `message` are the webapp's wire names (camelCase). Canonical home is mc-chat contract/ (subtree-shared to MCProxy); `category` is no longer part of a message.",
